# esc-owner.allow -- the places that name Esc outside the table of claims.
#
# Read by tests/check-esc-owner.sh, one line per place, three shapes:
#
#   K4|<kind>|<argument>|<file>|<holder>|<count>|<reason>
#       a string literal that holds the word Esc.  <holder> is the function
#       that holds it or the macro that names it, <count> how many such
#       strings that holder holds: more is a new promise nobody has read,
#       fewer is a stale line.
#   K5|<kind>|<file>|<function>|<count>|<reason>
#       a function that mentions WPE_ESC or CtrlC, or compares a key with a
#       numeric escape code.  <count> is the number of such mentions in its
#       body: a changed count is red until the function is read again.
#   K6|front|<what>|<reason>
#       a row of the table that claims the key in its own window only.
#
# K4 kinds: claim|<the row's what> -- the string is a claim's promise, and the
# table must have that row; loop|<function> -- a key loop of its own, where Esc
# closes the box, list or menu the user is in and ends no activity behind it;
# word|<symbol> -- a key's name, or a report of what a key did, not a promise.
# K5 kinds: loop| reads the key itself, result| reads or returns a box's result
# code, claim| belongs to the owner of the key, word| names the key's code
# (a binding, a decoder, an encoder) without acting on it.
#
# A line whose file, holder or function is not in the tree is red: the scan is
# blind, so a stale entry must not sit here quietly.
#
# The ten claims of the table (we_cancel.c), which the K4 claim| lines name:
#   the build, the debugger start, scala-cli setup, the build server,
#   the language server, the compile for debug, the debugger's answer,
#   the assistant's task, the assistant's turn, the chat pane.
#
# ---- K4: every string that holds the word Esc -----------------------------
K4|claim|the assistant's task|edit.h|E_SAY_ASSISTANT_BUSY|1|the line a locked window says when it refuses a key
K4|claim|the assistant's task|we_ai.c|AI_CLI_ENDS|1|what a stalled write to the assistant's child ends with
K4|claim|the assistant's turn|we_ai_host.c|HOST_ENDS|1|what a stalled write to the hosted engine ends with
K4|loop|ai_agent_approve|we_ai_ui.c|ai_agent_approve|1|the tool approval box: Esc is its deny
K4|claim|the chat pane|we_ai_ui.c|ai_agent_offer_follow_up|1|the pane's own hint that Esc leaves it
K4|word|ai_build_system|we_ai_ui.c|ai_build_system|1|text of the system prompt sent to the model, not a line the user reads
K4|claim|the chat pane|we_ai_ui.c|ai_chat_emit_hints_once|1|the pane's key hints, written once per pane
K4|claim|the assistant's turn|we_ai_ui.c|AI_CLEAR_REFUSED_LINE|1|the refusal of Clear conversation while a turn runs
K4|loop|ai_complete_ud_free|we_ai_ui.c|ai_complete_ud_free|1|the completion review box: Esc discards
K4|loop|ai_consent_gate|we_ai_ui.c|ai_consent_gate|1|the web-access consent box: Esc is not now
K4|loop|ai_diff_confirm_write|we_ai_ui.c|ai_diff_confirm_write|1|the write confirmation box: Esc is deny
K4|loop|ai_mp_key_listing|we_ai_ui.c|ai_listing_wait_open|2|the model list's own wait: Esc closes the list
K4|loop|ai_mp_key_listing|we_ai_ui.c|AI_MP_EARLY_LINE|1|the model list before it has anything to show
K4|loop|ai_mp_key_listing|we_ai_ui.c|AI_MP_HINT|1|the model list's key hints
K4|loop|ai_plan_choice|we_ai_ui.c|ai_plan_choice|1|the plan review box: Esc cancels
K4|loop|e_ai_prompt1|we_ai_ui.c|AI_PROMPT_LABEL|1|the assistant's prompt box: Esc is its Cancel
K4|loop|ai_diff_box_show|we_ai_ui.c|AI_SCOPE_BOX_HINT|1|the folder scope box: Esc is no
K4|loop|ai_diff_box_show|we_ai_ui.c|AI_SCOPE_BOX_HINT_ONCE|1|the folder scope box asked again: Esc is no
K4|claim|the assistant's task|we_ai_ui.c|ai_spin_cb|1|the task's spinner in the pane
K4|loop|ai_web_notice|we_ai_ui.c|AI_WEB_NOTICE_KEYS|1|the web notice box: Esc is not now
